{
  "summary": "This experiment tested a learned nonlinear RNA encoder (scvi_n200) in place of the linear PCA-2000 projection, holding modality (RNA-only), profile setting (multiprofile), and aggregation (avgpool) fixed relative to llm_summary_003 to isolate the encoder effect. Validation accuracy improved to ~0.650 (F1: ~0.628) from ~0.591 (F1: ~0.573) under PCA-2000, indicating in this clean single-variable comparison that the learned encoder captures structure beyond what the linear projection provides. It remains uncertain whether this encoder advantage generalizes to alternative aggregation strategies or persists when the RNA branch is combined with the image modality in multimodal fusion settings, and whether other learned encoders or latent dimensions could yield further gains."
}

